# ---------------- Cyrus Poonawalla
OPEN='https://openthemagazine.com/feature/the-legend-of-the-poonawallas'
WSI='https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serum_Institute_of_India'
add('cyrus-poonawalla','mixed',
 'Cyrus Poonawalla founded Serum Institute (1966) and is its chairman; his son Adar Poonawalla is CEO and was the public face of Covishield. The only documented state transaction in the reviewed record is company-level: in 2021 the government bought Covishield at a subsidised price and advanced Rs 3,000 crore to Serum for purchases. The reporting is mostly about Adar and the company, describes a strained government relationship, and records no personal exchange by Cyrus. The one personal item is a Parsi-community vaccine-reservation request that Cyrus offered to meet; its outcome is not documented. No rubric.',
 'Company-level government vaccine procurement and advance; personal exchange not established',
 'Covid vaccine procurement 2020–2021',
 [r('Open magazine (updated 9 July 2021): the government advanced Rs 3,000 crore to Serum in April 2021 and bought doses at a "highly subsidised rate of around US$2 per dose"; the government took over distribution and temporarily banned exports. The piece is a profile of the family. It shows Cyrus only in a 2013 photo with Pranab Mukherjee and describes no party affiliation.','Open magazine: The Legend of the Poonawallas',OPEN,'2021-07-09','Reported company-government transaction (secondary)','Page text reviewed via fetch summary'),
  r('Lists Cyrus Poonawalla as founder and Chairman and MD and Adar as CEO, the company\'s Covishield programme and the reported August 2020 price estimate of about Rs 225 a dose. Does not cover the 2021 purchases or any political links.','Wikipedia: Serum Institute of India',WSI,'2026','Role attribution (tertiary)',WIKI)],
 [r('The same Open feature says the dose price was roughly a tenth of the global average, relations with the government became strained, the Poonawallas "seem to have unfortunately become scapegoats" for delayed government orders, and the government retook control of procurement in June. Adar describes unprecedented pressure and the financial risk taken on early production. Cyrus said "I am proud of spending the money with which I have enriched myself." Adar supported his father\'s offer to reserve 60,000 vials for Parsis, which he said was about a day\'s production.','Open magazine',OPEN,'2021-07-09','Alternative explanation, subject responses and limits','Page text reviewed via fetch summary'),
  r('Discovery leads on Panama Papers property attachments of relatives and Serum donation channels were not readable and are not used. No relative\'s or company\'s case is attributed to Cyrus.','Not relied on',OPEN,'2021-07-09','Explicit limit of evidence','Not applicable')],
 'Identity: Serum\'s 2021 purchase, price and advance concern the company and Adar; Cyrus is chairman and founder. Not verified from primary records: the advance\'s terms, price per dose, Serum\'s electoral contributions, Parliament Q&A or PIB statements. The Open article is a single secondary account. Public-health procurement in an emergency has legitimate purposes; no wrongdoing found or alleged by the sources. Not exoneration.')

